WEBVTT

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:32.538
So I think that the things that we're
seeing now are very much glimpse of

00:06:32.579 --> 00:06:34.996
the future. We released three,

00:06:35.288 --> 00:06:39.788
which is a general-purpose natural
language text model in

00:06:39.996 --> 00:06:41.121
the summer of twenty twenty.

00:06:41.663 --> 00:06:44.496
You know, there's hundreds of applications
that are now using it in

00:06:44.496 --> 00:06:46.663
production that's ramping
up all of the time.

00:06:47.121 --> 00:06:51.329
But there are things where people
use three to really understand

00:06:51.329 --> 00:06:54.704
the intent behind the search
query and deliver results

00:06:54.704 --> 00:06:57.038
and sort of understand not only intent,

00:06:57.038 --> 00:06:59.788
but all of the data and deliver
the thing of what you want.

00:06:59.788 --> 00:07:03.454
So you can sort of describe a fuzzy thing
and it'll understand documents.